he pre-state file create a TOCTOU window between posture-check variables, PUT body, and audit log; and the workflow invokes check-invocation-log-entry.sh from checked-out PR code enabling a self-modifying bypass. R1-SB-004 (single-char cohort detection) and R1-SB-005 (staged prior-restore test) carry forward. D-047 trust-model claim 'restore verified' remains overstated until TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 closes.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Restore-mode context verify uses grep -Fq (substring) not set-equality. A live state that is a superset of the restored contexts passes verify silently and emits 'verification passed ✓'. Carry-forward from R20 R1-SB-001; TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 tracks closure to extras-2.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 873-880: restore branch 'if ! printf %s $CHECKS_CONTEXTS | grep -Fq -- $EXPECTED_CHECKS_CONTEXTS'. Forward-mode else-branch at line 883 uses exact equality '[ $CHECKS_CONTEXTS = $EXPECTED_CHECKS_CONTEXTS ]'. The asymmetry is unchanged from R20. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 in STATUS.md carries this forward.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Post-restore state carrying additional required-status-check contexts passes verification undetected. D-047 trust-model claim that restore is verified implies exact fidelity; the subset check makes that claim overstated. Operator reviewing the log sees 'passed' but posture may differ from the intended pre-state.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Replace grep -Fq with sorted set-equality (sort|comm or Python set compare). Deferred to 024B-extras-2 via TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001. Until closure, add a §12.8 caveat that the verify step is subset-only and the operator should confirm context equality via jq after restore.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\