lls 'scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh' with no path-pinning. The Checkout step (line 30) checks out the PR's HEAD. A PR modifying scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh to exit 0 unconditionally would pass the check-invocation-log-entry required-status-check on its own merge PR.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"In the current D-031 single-operator context, blast radius is bounded (the operator already has full admin access). For future multi-operator adoption, any contributor could self-bypass cascade-status enforcement by including a script modification in the same PR. This converts the required-status-check from a hard gate to a soft one.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Pin the enforcement step to run the script from the base branch (origin/main), not the PR HEAD: 'git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...'. Alternatively, use a reusable workflow pinned by SHA that calls the base-branch version. Low urgency under D-031 but required before multi-operator adoption.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Cohort dispatch-note preference in the resolve-dispatch step uses grep -E '024[C-F]/DISPATCH-NOTE.md$' — a single-character-only match. A future multi-char cohort ID (e.g. 024C-2) would not be recognised as a cohort note; the head -n1 fallback on all_dispatch_notes would prefer a tooling note in a mixed PR, causing enforcement to exit 0 silently. Carry-forward from R20 R1-SB-004.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml resolve-dispatch step line 59: 'grep -E ^docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-F]/DISPATCH-NOTE.md$'. all_dispatch_notes uses '024[A-Za-z][^/]*' (multi-char flexible). If a PR contains both 024G/DISPATCH-NOTE.md (tooling) and 024C-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md (hypothetical cohort), cohort_dispatch_note would be empty, head -n1 fallback selects 024G, tooling case triggers, enforcement skipped.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Low urgency for the current 5-cohort set (024C–F, all single-char). Becomes a bypass surface if a multi-char cohort sub-slice (e.g. 024C-retrial) is introduced without updating the regex and tooling case list simultaneously.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Widen cohort detection to '024[C-F][^/]*/DISPATCH-NOTE.md$' (allows multi-char suffix). Update tooling case statement to '024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G)' with a trailing comment noting the pattern must not match 024[C-F]* prefixes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Test harness validates prior_restore_evidence_present only for unstaged working-tree changes; no test covers staged (git-added but uncommitted) restore entries, leaving a regression surface if git diff HEAD is ever narrowed to git diff. Carry-forward from R20 R1-SB-005.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh lines 3153-3220: enable-working-tree-prior-restore writes the restore entry to branch-protection-log.md without calling 'git add' before run_enable_case. git diff HEAD correctly covers staged changes by semantics, but the test does not exercise this path. No subsequent test calls 'git -C repo_dir add branch-protection-log.md' before asserting exit 2.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A future developer who changes 'git diff HEAD' to 'git diff' (unstaged only) in prior_restore_evidence_present would not be caught by the test suite, silently regressing R8-SAFE-002 closure for staged entries.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a test variant that calls 'git -C $repo_dir add docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md' after writing restore evidence and before run_enable_case, asserting exit 2 with the uncommitted-evidence message. One additional test case in the existing enable-working-tree section.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"carry_forward_verified\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-SAFE-001\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification escape hatch concern\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"N/A\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"--expected-wrapper-sha and Gate 2 automated verification carved to 024B-extras-2. No escape hatch exists in this slice. §12.8 WARNING and CAUTION blocks present as specified.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-SAFE-002\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Working-tree prior-entry detection misses uncommitted Gate-1 entries\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"prior_restore_evidence_present uses git diff HEAD which covers staged and unstaged changes. in_block is only set by added +### lines (diff + stripped); removed -### lines remain prefixed and do not match ^### . False-positive and false-negative behaviour verified correct.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-Bootstrap\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Workflow self-blocks introducing slice's own PR\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"paths: 024[C-Z]*/** naturally excludes 024A/024B-*. STATUS.md trigger handled by tooling case statement exit-0 short-circuit. 024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md matches tooling case.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R20-R1-SB-002\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"§12.8 Gate 3 SOP missing extended-breakage flag documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"§12.8 Gate 3 now reads: 'If the wrapper has had no successful runs in the past 60 days due to extended pre-Gate-2 breakage, append --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci.' Closes the operator incident-scenario gap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R20-R1-SB-003\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Absent enforce_admins.enabled key silently coerces to false\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json lines 376-378 now explicitly check 'if enabled not in enforce_admins' and exit 2 with clear error. Real GitHub API always includes the key; guard handles manually-crafted files.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counts\\\": {\\n    \\\"CRIT\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"MAJ\\\": 1,\\n    \\\"MIN\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"nit\\\": 1\\n  }\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"42100b41-8358-43ba-80e3-d04fe5d75295\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.59576635,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":19,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":121991,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1404047,\"output_tokens\":47681,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":121991,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":14716,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":123904,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5468,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":5468},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1669,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0018139999999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":19,\"outputTokens\":47681,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1404047,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":121991,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.59395235,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"15cb63b3-8966-442f-bb69-dace2f2c37d6\"}\n\n---FILE---\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":508417,\"duration_api_ms\":509719,\"num_turns\":27,\"result\":\"Now I have sufficient evidence to produce the review. Let me compile the findings.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-1\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\n  \\\"round\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"024B-extras-1 is structurally complete under the completeness_governance lens. Every DISPATCH-NOTE AC maps to a concrete artefact: --restore mode implemented; forward-mode path-pinned safety check wired; ADOPT-001 §12.8 3-gate break-glass procedure present with mandatory MUST language and WARNING/CAUTION callouts; check-invocation-log-entry.yml wired with correct paths-filter, SHA-pinned action, and tooling-slice short-circuit; restore tests present (run_restore_case + make_restore_fake_gh); D-047 filed as ACCEPTED with date 2026-05-10, covering all extras-1 deliverables, acknowledging --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification deferral to D-048/extras-2, and noting bootstrap paths-ignore via tooling-slice short-circuiting. Step-7 merge-blocking AC is correctly unchecked: placeholder exists at restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md, TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 has a formal STATUS.md bullet row with clear closure criteria, and the DISPATCH-NOTE AC list leaves it unchecked. Carry-forward findings are correctly routed: R8-CORR-001/003 closed in 024B-core; R8-CORR-002 addressed via prior_restore_evidence_present() scoped to forward-mode only; R8-SAFE-001 mitigated via §12.8 WARNING/CAUTION + D-047 rationale; R8-SAFE-002 addressed via git diff HEAD check; R8 bootstrap closed via 024[C-Z]** paths filter + tooling-slice case block. VERSIONING.md lists all 7 extras-1 flags (6 posture-degradation + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci) plus --restore. Plan-doc §6 024C gate conditions (024B-extras-1 merge + TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001 + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001) are correctly documented. Anti-descoping is honoured: extras-2 surface explicitly carved with SCOPE-CORRECTION-2 doc, D-048 reservation, TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 formal row, and no silent scope reduction. Three low-severity gaps follow.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CMP-R1-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Four TFs (TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001, TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001, TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001, TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001) are described as 'filed' in the 2026-05-11 chain entry row 4 but have no formal bullet rows in the STATUS.md tracked-forward items section (lines 316-324).\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md chain entry 2026-05-11 row 4: 'Deferred low-risk follow-ups filed for extras-2 / step-7 tracking: [four TF IDs].' The §'Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras' section contains 6 items; none of the four named TFs appears there. TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001 is step-7 scoped but not extras-2 scoped, so it will not be automatically picked up by the 024B-extras-2 dispatch.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Chain entries compress under context limits. Without formal TF rows the three extras-2 items may not be included in 024B-extras-2's dispatch scope, and TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001 (step-7 fixture sequencing) has no canonical closure path entry. Operators consulting the TF list will not see these four items.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add four bullet rows to the tracked-forward items section. For the three extras-2 items: 'Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice dispatch; does NOT gate 024C.' For TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001: 'Fixture sequencing concern for the step-7 demo; non-blocking; closes when step-7 evidence sequence is validated by operator.' Closure paths already implicit in extras-2 SCOPE-CORRECTION-2 and step-7 PLACEHOLDER; entries just need formal discoverability.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CMP-R1-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The step-7 evidence placeholder step 6 lists 'timestamps, _links, url' as API envelope fields to exclude from the jq verification comparison but omits 'contexts_url', which the DISPATCH-NOTE explicitly names and the script's transform() function strips.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE scope table step-7 entry: 'stripping envelope fields (timestamps, _links, url, contexts_url)'. restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md step 6: 'API envelope fields (timestamps, _links, url) differ and should be excluded.' enable-required-check.sh transform() at the Python helper: strips keys in {'_links', 'url', 'checks', 'required_signatures', 'enforcement_level', 'contexts_url'} and any key ending in '_url'.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Operator following the placeholder literally may include contexts_url in the comparison, causing a spurious mismatch on a non-state field and either rejecting valid evidence or committing evidence that documents an apparent discrepancy requiring explanation.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"In placeholder step 6, update the envelope exclusion list to: 'API envelope fields (timestamps, _links, url, contexts_url, and any key ending in _url) differ and should be excluded from the jq comparison.' Matches DISPATCH-NOTE and script behaviour.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CMP-R1-nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 WARNING correctly defers automated --expected-wrapper-sha verification to 024B-extras-2 and cites SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md, but provides no trackable TF or D-NNN cross-reference for operators to follow up on when extras-2 lands.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"§12.8 Gate 3 WARNING: 'Automated --expected-wrapper-sha verification is deferred to slice 024B-extras-2 (see docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). In 024B-extras-1 the operator MUST manually verify...' No TF reference. SCOPE-CORRECTION-2 is a rationale document, not a TF closure marker. D-048 (reserved for extras-2) is cited only in DECISIONS.md, not in §12.8.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Operators reading §12.8 after extras-2 merges cannot determine from the in-text deferral note whether the upgrade has landed. The SCOPE-CORRECTION-2 file is a historical rationale artefact, not a live tracking pointer.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Append to the Gate 3 WARNING: 'Tracked at D-048 (DECISIONS.md); check STATUS.md TF section for 024B-extras-2 closure.' Alternately, when 024B-extras-2 files its own TF for wrapper-SHA verification, back-reference §12.8's deferral note with that TF ID.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"20c8d42f-ef13-41d8-be5e-a44feaf615bb\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.05720945,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":14,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":102229,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":821369,\"output_tokens\":28363,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":102229,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":16668,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":100150,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":9460,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":9460},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1823,\"outputTokens\":26,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0019529999999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":14,\"outputTokens\":28363,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":821369,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":102229,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.05525645,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"935dfbfe-15bf-4fd6-a517-215635693d95\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
